        Root cause:
        The root cause of the bug appears to be related to the improper handling of alarm state changes and database updates. The previous implementation relied on the `changeAlarm` method, which was responsible for both updating the alarm in the database and managing the in-memory set of alarms. This complexity likely led to inconsistencies in the alarm state, particularly when enabling or disabling alarms, as well as when deleting them. The refactoring aimed to simplify these operations and ensure that the state of alarms is consistently updated in both the in-memory structure and the database.

